.TH THEREMINI-CTL 1 "2026-07-28" "ThereMaxi" "ThereMaxi Manual"
.SH NAME
theremini-ctl \- control a Moog Theremini from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B theremini-ctl
.RI [ --channel " N" ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B theremini-ctl
drives a Moog Theremini over ALSA MIDI without a graphical display, so the
device can be operated from a script or over an SSH session. It exposes the same
operations the ThereMaxi editor performs: identifying the device, detecting the
antenna channel, backing up and restoring presets, renaming a slot, pushing a
single parameter live, sending a preset from a
.I .theremaxi
library into a device slot, and pulling every device preset into a library file.
.PP
Unless a command says otherwise it first discovers the Theremini on the ALSA
sequencer and connects to it, printing
.B connected to:
and the client name. If no device is present the command prints a message to
standard error and exits non-zero.
.PP
Slots and preset numbers are 1-based, matching the numbers shown on the device
(1 to 32).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --channel " N"
The MIDI channel (0\(en15) used by the commands that write to the device
.RB ( set ", " send-preset ", " restore ", " set-name ).
Defaults to 0, which is correct for a factory-configured device. Must appear
before the command.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Device commands
These need a connected Theremini.
.TP
.B identify
Connect and print the firmware version. This is the default when no command is
given.
.TP
.B detect
Watch the antenna stream and print the MIDI channel it uses. Move a hand near
the antennas so the device streams while this runs.
.TP
.B dump
Fetch the preset dump and print how many presets it contains. Nothing is
written to disk.
.TP
.BI backup " file.syx"
Fetch the preset dump and save its raw bytes to
.IR file.syx .
Take one of these before any command that writes to the device, so a slot can
be put back with
.BR restore .
.TP
.BI restore " slot file.syx"
Write the preset stored for
.I slot
in a backup made with
.B backup
back to that slot on the device. This overwrites the slot.
.TP
.BI set-name " slot name"
Select
.IR slot ,
set its preset name to
.IR name ,
and save it on the device.
.TP
.BI set " cc value"
Send one parameter live. If
.I cc
is a known parameter's controller number,
.I value
is interpreted in that parameter's display units (Hz, %, ms, semitones, an enum
index) and converted to the wire form \(em including the two messages a 14-bit
parameter needs. For an unknown
.IR cc ,
.I value
is sent straight through, clamped to 0\(en127. See
.B params
for the controller numbers.
.TP
.BI send-preset " lib n " [ --slot " slot" ]
Read preset number
.I n
from the
.I .theremaxi
library
.I lib
and write it to
.I slot
on the device. Without
.BR --slot ,
the preset goes to the slot with the same number as
.IR n .
This overwrites the target slot.
.TP
.BI sync " lib.theremaxi"
Fetch every preset from the device and save them as the
.I .theremaxi
library
.IR lib.theremaxi ,
overwriting that file. This is the reverse of
.BR send-preset :
it pulls the device into a file the ThereMaxi editor can open.
.SS Offline commands
These do not touch the device.
.TP
.B params
List every parameter: its id, controller number, name, and either its numeric
range or that it is an enum or a text field.
.TP
.B help
Print a usage summary. \fB--help\fR and \fB-h\fR do the same.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command ran but failed \(em no device, a bad reply, an unreadable file, an
out-of-range slot.
.TP
.B 2
The command line could not be parsed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Identify the connected device:
.PP
.RS
.EX
theremini-ctl identify
.EE
.RE
.PP
Find out which channel the antennas use:
.PP
.RS
.EX
theremini-ctl detect
.EE
.RE
.PP
Back up every preset before changing anything:
.PP
.RS
.EX
theremini-ctl backup ~/theremini-factory.syx
.EE
.RE
.PP
Put slot 5 back the way the backup has it:
.PP
.RS
.EX
theremini-ctl restore 5 ~/theremini-factory.syx
.EE
.RE
.PP
Set the filter cutoff (CC 74) to 42% live:
.PP
.RS
.EX
theremini-ctl set 74 42
.EE
.RE
.PP
Send the third preset of a library to device slot 10:
.PP
.RS
.EX
theremini-ctl send-preset mysounds.theremaxi 3 --slot 10
.EE
.RE
.PP
Pull the whole device into a library file:
.PP
.RS
.EX
theremini-ctl sync device-backup.theremaxi
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I *.theremaxi
Preset libraries in the JSON format shared with the ThereMaxi editor and the
original Perl application.
.TP
.I *.syx
Raw sysex preset dumps written by
.BR backup .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR theremini-probe (1),
the ThereMaxi editor, and
.B DESIGN.md
in the source tree for the protocol details.
